<!--META-DATA
{
	tags: ["for", "while", "mod"],
}
-->

<statement>
	<p>
		Return <pf>true</pf> if a given number is automorphic and <pf>false</pf> otherwise.
	</p>

	<p>
		A number <m>N</m> is <em>automorphic</em> if <m>N^2</m> ends with the digits of <m>N</m>.
	</p>

	<p>
		For instance, <m>5</m> is automorphic because <m>5^2 = 25</m> ends with <m>5</m>, and <m>376</m> is automorphic because <m>376^2 = 141376</m> ends with <m>376</m>.
	</p>

	<tabular valign="top" halign="right" top="minor">
		<col width="12%"/>
		<col width="88%" halign="left"/>
		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell>Inputs:</cell>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>num</pf> (1 x 1) integer</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell>Outputs:</cell>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>result</pf> (1 x 1) logical — <pf>true</pf> if <pf>num</pf> is automorphic, <pf>false</pf> otherwise..</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
		<row>
			<cell>Details:</cell>
			<cell>
				<p>Use a loop to determine how many digits are in <pf>num</pf>. (Hint: repeatedly divide by ten until the value is less than 1.)</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
		<row>
			<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p>Use the digit count with <pf>mod</pf> to extract the trailing digits of <pf>num^2</pf>.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p>Compare the extracted digits to <pf>num</pf> to determine the result.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
	</tabular>

	<p>
	Examples:
	<program>
		<code>
			result = is_automorphic(110)
			% should return
			% result = 0   % logical false
		</code>
	</program>
	<program>
		<code>
			result = is_automorphic(76)
			% should return
			% result = 1   % logical true
		</code>
	</program>
	</p>
</statement>
